# Focus Sentinel — ignore rules
#
# Two kinds of entry live here:
#   1. NEVER-COMMIT — programme machinery and evidence (charter commit policy).
#   2. Build artefacts — regenerable output of the toolchain.
#
# What is deliberately NOT ignored, because it is committed source:
#   FocusSentinel.xcodeproj/                  hand-authored, never generated (R-01)
#   Focus.xcworkspace/                        the unit lane lives here (P-15/P-16)
#   */xcshareddata/                           shared schemes are the lane definitions
#   Packages/*/Tests/*/Resources/             test fixtures (P-35)
#   Packages/*/Tests/*/__Snapshots__/         snapshot baselines (R-10)
#   App/Assets.xcassets/                      the rendered app icon

# --- NEVER COMMIT: programme machinery (charter commit policy) ---
.agents/
explainers/
.beads/
.claude/
.codex/
*.log

# --- Build products and local toolchain state ---
build/
DerivedData/
.build/
# …and `.build` itself, which on this machine is a SYMLINK into a shared build cache.
# `.build/` matches a directory only, so the symlink was invisible to it and eight of them
# were committed by a `git add -A` before this line existed (focus-0nm).
.build
*.xcresult
*.xcuserstate
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserdatad/
Packages/*/.swiftpm/
.swiftpm/
Tools/*/.swiftpm/

# --- macOS noise ---
.DS_Store
